course: dictionary
lesson: 2361
title: Cuddle and cwtch: words of comfort
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Cuddle can be a verb or a noun. As a verb, to cuddle someone is to hold them close in your arms to show love or comfort them. As a noun, a cuddle is a long, warm hug. «Dad and his partner have a baby, and Teddy sees Dad cuddling her and feels replaced.» Dad is holding the baby close, so cuddling is the action he does.
explain: Look at the words around a word to find its meaning. «Mia hid Gran's broken china cat; Gran wasn't sad about the cat, only that Mia hadn't told her, and gave her a cwtch, the Welsh word for a cuddle.» Gran gave a hug after Mia said sorry, and the sentence tells you cwtch is the Welsh word for a cuddle.
explain: Cuddle up is a phrase. To cuddle up is to lie or sit close to someone to be warm and comfortable. Try your meaning in the sentence instead of the word. If "hold close to be warm" fits, your meaning is right.
fact: To cuddle someone means to hold them close in your arms to show love or to comfort them.
fact: A cuddle is a long, warm hug. A cuddly toy is one you like to hug.
fact: «Cwtch» means a cuddle in Wales, so Gran's hug was a cwtch.
fact: Cuddles should feel safe. You can always say no to a cuddle you do not want, even from family, and a grown-up you trust can help you.
fact: In Ohio, several children cuddled backyard chickens and got Salmonella, so always wash your hands after touching animals.
exercise: «Dad and his partner have a baby, and Teddy sees Dad cuddling her and feels replaced.» What is Dad doing? | Putting her in the bath | Shouting at the baby to be quiet | *Holding her close in his arms to show love | Counting her toes
exercise: «Gran wanted a cuddle before bed.» Is cuddle a noun or a verb in this sentence? | *Noun | Verb | Adjective | Adverb
exercise: «Mia hid Gran's broken china cat; Gran gave her a cwtch, the Welsh word for a cuddle.» What does cwtch mean? | *A cuddle | A ticket | A broken cat | A scolding
test: Your friend asks for a cuddle, but you do not want one. What does the body safety lesson say? | Family can always make you hug them | Cuddles are only for babies | *You can say no to a cuddle you do not want, even from family | You must hug anyone who asks
test: What does "cuddle up" mean? | To fall over | *To lie or sit close to someone to be warm and comfortable | To shout loudly | To wash up after dinner
exam: How can you check your meaning of cuddle in «Teddy sees Dad cuddling her and feels replaced»? | Look it up in a cookbook | Skip the whole sentence and guess | Ask the baby what it means | *Put "holding close" into the sentence and see if it still makes sense
